{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PHM",
  "chapter": 1,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Paul, a prisoner of Jesus Christ, and Timothy ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "our",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " brother, to Philemon our dearly beloved, and fellow-laborer,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "our",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " beloved Apphia, and Archippus our fellow-soldier, and to the church in thy house:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Grace to you, and peace, from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I thank my God, making mention of thee always in my prayers,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hearing of thy love and faith, which thou hast towards the Lord Jesus, and towards all saints;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That the communication of thy faith may become effectual by the acknowledging of every good thing which is in you in Christ Jesus.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we have great joy and consolation in thy love, because the bowels of the saints are refreshed by thee, brother.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore, though I might be very bold in Christ to enjoin thee that which is convenient.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet for love's sake I rather beseech ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", being such one as Paul the aged, and now also a prisoner of Jesus Christ.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I beseech thee for my son Onesimus, whom I have begotten in my bonds:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who in time past was to thee unprofitable, but now profitable to thee and to me:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whom I have sent again: thou therefore receive him, that is, my own bowels:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whom I would have retained with me, that in thy stead he might have ministered to me in the bonds of the gospel:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But without thy mind I would do nothing; that thy benefit should not be as it were of necessity, but willingly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For perhaps he therefore departed for a season, that thou shouldst receive him for ever;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Not now as a servant, but above a servant, a brother beloved, specially to me, but how much more to thee, both in the flesh, and in the Lord?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If thou accountest me therefore a partner, receive him as myself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If he hath wronged thee, or oweth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " aught, put that on my account;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I Paul have written ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with my own hand, I will repay ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": although I do not say to thee that thou owest to me even thy own self besides.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, brother, let me have joy of thee in the Lord: refresh my bowels in the Lord.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Having confidence in thy obedience I wrote to thee, knowing that thou wilt also do more than I say.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But at the same time prepare me also a lodging; for I trust that through your prayers I shall be given to you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There salute thee Epaphras, my fellow-prisoner in Christ Jesus;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Marcus, Aristarchus, Demas, Lucas, my fellow-laborers.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHM.1.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHM.1.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with your spirit. Amen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
